# Line endings are LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Every text file here is written by a formatter that emits LF — prettier,
# rustfmt, gofmt, ruff. Checking out CRLF meant each format run rewrote what git
# had just translated, so files showed as modified with an empty diff. There are
# no Windows-native scripts in this repository to want CRLF.
#
# Order matters: later rules win, so the exceptions below must stay below this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never translated, never diffed as text. `text=auto` detects most of
# these anyway; naming them makes a misdetection impossible.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary

# Files whose exact bytes matter.
#
# Pack manifests are compared byte-for-byte across platforms: the same payload
# must produce the same manifest on a developer machine and on CI. The global
# rule above already pins them; this stays as the explicit statement of why, so
# relaxing the global rule cannot silently break determinism.
app/src-tauri/packs-baseline/**/manifest.json text eol=lf

# Signed TUF metadata and the fixture repository are verified against signatures
# over their bytes. Any line-ending translation invalidates them, so nothing here
# is treated as text — this must remain the last word.
app/src-tauri/tests/fixtures/** -text
